{
 "_meta": {
  "title": "ListingDoctor – category word lists (proposal)",
  "as_of": "2026-10-22",
  "rules_reference": "code/shared/references/rules.md section 10 (IDs CB*, CE*, CT*, CF*, CA*)",
  "status": "proposal, not yet wired into ld_rules.py · integrated in ListingDoctor 1.1.0 (message_de added, CB7-inci-missing added)",
  "matching": "case-insensitive, Unicode NFC, whole phrase on word boundaries; hyphen/space variants are listed explicitly; regex = Python re with re.IGNORECASE unless 'case_sensitive': true",
  "fields": "item_name, title_differentiation (Item Highlights), bullet_point1-5, product_description; generic_keyword for CF9 disease/drug terms",
  "language_market": "en lists target amazon.com (US law + Amazon US policy); de lists target amazon.de / EU law. English text on an EU store: run the en lists as warning only.",
  "global_lists": "The section-5 lists in ld_rules.py (PROMO_*, HEALTH, ECO, EVIDENCE, SUBJECTIVE) still apply to every category. Phrases already there are not repeated here (e.g. 'fda approved', 'clinically proven', 'detox', 'immune system', 'hypoallergenic', 'klinisch getestet', 'stärkt das immunsystem', 'behandelt', 'heilt').",
  "category_detection": "1) product_type of the category listing report (uppercase, e.g. HAIRBAND in a real 2026 DE report); 2) fallback product_words for pasted text, like TEXTILE_WORDS.",
  "product_types_note": "Product-type names are partly unverified: SKIN_MOISTURIZER and HAIR_STYLING_AGENT seen in a seller forum, the rest from Amazon naming conventions. Verify with the SP-API Product Type Definitions API (searchDefinitionsProductTypes) or real reports; unknown names simply never match.",
  "conditional_semantics": "A 'conditional' block is only evaluated if at least one 'if_any' phrase occurs in the listing text.",
  "pattern_semantics": "pattern: hit if 'regex' matches; if 'requires_missing' is set, hit only if that regex does NOT match anywhere in the listing; if 'if_regex' is set, both must match.",
  "disclaimer": "Checklist, not legal advice."
 },
